<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. Above FR have been reviewed by the Audit Com at its meeting held on 13.2.21 and approved by the Board of Directors (Board) at their meeting held on that date. The Statutory Auditor has reviewed the same.2. The above reviewed FR of the Group [IFGL Refractories Ltd &amp; 14 subsidiaries] have been prepared in accordance with Ind AS notified under the Companies (IND AS) Rules, 15 as amended by the Companies (IND AS) (Amendment) Rules, 16. These FR have been prepared in accordance with the recgnitn &amp; measrment principles of Ind AS - 34 - IFR, prescribed under Sec 133 of the CA, 2013 read with the relevant rules issued thereunder &amp; the other acctng principles generally accepted in India. 3. The Group is engaged in the business of manufacture, trading and sale of refractories and is managed organisationally as a single unit. The Group has adopted geographical location of its operations (where its products are produced or service rendering activities are based) as its operating segment in terms of Ind AS 108(OS). 4. A scheme of amalgamation of erstwhile IFGL Refractories Ltd. with the Holding Co w.e.f 1.04.16 was approved by the Hon’ble NCLT, Kol vide order 3.8.17. Goodwill of Rs. 26,699 lakhs arose on such merger which was accounted for under Purchase Method as defined under erstwhile AS 14(Acctng for Amalgamtion). Useful life of such Goodwill was estimated to be 10 yrs and it is being amortised.5. The Holding Co’s Writ Petition No. 544 of 2019 challenging vires of the Explanation to Sect 10AA(1) of the IT Act, 1961 inserted on and from A.Y beginning 01.4.18, on grounds that such explanation denies the benefit that was intended to be provided under the said sec, was admitted by the Hon’ble HC at Cal on 07.11.19. Supported by a legal opinion obtained in this regard, mgt believes that the Holding Co has a good case on merit in this matter and the resultant deferred tax assets of Rs. 1,164 lakhs are considered as recoverable in future.6. The outbreak of COVID-19 pandemic globally is causing significant disturbance and slowdown of eco activities. In many countries, businesses are being forced to cease or limit their operations for long or indefinite period. Measures taken to contain the spread of the virus, including travel bans, quarantines, social distancing, and closures of non-essential services have triggered significant disruptions to businesses worldwide, resulting in an economic slowdown &amp; uncertainties pertaining to future operations of their businesses. The Grp resumed its business activities after a brief disruption in certain components and there has been continuous improvement in the operations since then. The Grp mgt has assessed the operations and liquidity position of the Grp taking into consideration improvement in the steel sector. Based on such assessment, the Grp mgt does not anticipate any challenge in the Group's ability to meet its financial obligations. However, the above evaluations are based on scenario analysis of internal &amp; external information available up to the date of approval of these FR.7. During the qtr, the obligation of the Grp’s entities operating in the USA to repay loans obtained by them from the govt of that country under the Paycheck Protection Program has been waived as per terms of the said program. Accordingly, such loans aggregating Rs.791 lakhs(equi to US$ 10,72,300)have been reversed &amp; recognised as Other Inc in FR.8. During the PY, the Group had recognised impairment loss amt to Rs 2,061 lakhs, which has been disclosed as an exceptional item in these consolidated FR.This impairment loss represented the write-down of carrying value of goodwill to the recoverable amt pertaining to German operations (IFGL GmbH and its step-down subsidiaries). The recoverable amt was based on value in use calculations using present value of future cash flows estimated by the mgt &amp; was determined at the level of CGU which consists of the assets of IFGL GmbH &amp; its step-down subsidiaries.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
